WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.606
A hundred and sixty-five million parameters, and a window of a hundred

00:00:04.606 --> 00:00:05.992
and twenty-eight thousand tokens.

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:10.950
Trained by reward alone after pretraining, for about four thousand two hundred dollars.

00:00:13.082 --> 00:00:14.049
Hi, I'm Pipkin.

00:00:14.049 --> 00:00:16.948
I read quark's config, its weights and its report.

00:00:20.558 --> 00:00:23.316
Sixteen layers, seven hundred and sixty-eight wide.

00:00:23.736 --> 00:00:26.748
Three local layers, then one global, four times over.

00:00:26.748 --> 00:00:29.759
Only the global layers look at the whole context.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.646
A local layer sees a short window, with a small convolution beside it.

00:00:35.646 --> 00:00:36.998
Its memory never grows.

00:00:37.418 --> 00:00:39.694
A global layer sees everything before it.

00:00:39.694 --> 00:00:42.620
Twelve query heads share four key and value heads.

00:00:43.992 --> 00:00:48.185
Attention and the convolution run side by side, and a learned weight blends them.

00:00:48.566 --> 00:00:50.851
The global layer is plain grouped-query attention.

00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:53.135
Its cache is the one that grows.

00:00:54.475 --> 00:00:59.258
Pretraining ran five hundred billion tokens on one eight-GPU node, the context

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:00.852
growing stage by stage.

00:01:01.252 --> 00:01:06.284
The thirty-two thousand token stage was mostly synthetic retrieval and tracking tasks.

00:01:06.684 --> 00:01:09.931
Then a branch trained at a hundred and twenty-eight thousand.

00:01:09.931 --> 00:01:14.152
The global layers' rotary base went from five hundred thousand to four million.

00:01:15.342 --> 00:01:17.917
About half a gigabyte of cache at full length.

00:01:17.917 --> 00:01:21.064
Make every layer global and it is about ten times more.

00:01:22.617 --> 00:01:24.064
Reinforcement learning used GRPO.

00:01:24.064 --> 00:01:27.681
Each prompt gets a group of replies, checked by code.

00:01:27.681 --> 00:01:30.575
If they all fail, the group teaches nothing.

00:01:30.995 --> 00:01:32.180
One success is enough.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:35.735
The passing reply is pushed up and the failures are pushed down.

00:01:36.155 --> 00:01:38.526
One harness never produced a valid call.

00:01:38.526 --> 00:01:41.574
With no success to compare against, it never learned.

00:01:41.994 --> 00:01:45.904
Harnesses added late started near half solved in their first hundred steps,

00:01:45.904 --> 00:01:48.184
so almost every group carried a signal.

00:01:49.908 --> 00:01:54.576
Across fifteen emulated coding harnesses, simple terminal tasks went from under three

00:01:54.576 --> 00:01:56.909
percent solved to about two thirds.

00:01:57.289 --> 00:01:59.580
These are training rollouts, not a held-out test.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.070
I ran both models on arithmetic.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:07.447
The base already got thirty-nine of forty prompts right somewhere in sixteen tries.

00:02:07.447 --> 00:02:09.467
RL made it right more often.

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.824
It sharpened a skill that was there.

00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:15.856
The base model already wrote tool calls.

00:02:15.856 --> 00:02:19.923
Offered a calculator, it called it nineteen times in twenty, with a

00:02:19.923 --> 00:02:21.279
placeholder for the argument.

00:02:21.699 --> 00:02:25.948
The RL objective kept a small supervised term, on steps written by code.

00:02:26.368 --> 00:02:30.176
And no fine-tuned model of the same size was run on the same tasks.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.417
Pretraining planted the tool format.

00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:38.141
Reward turned a handful of right answers into a skill, on simple tasks.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:43.010
Four layers that look far, a bigger rotary base, and reward

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.277
that needs one success.

00:02:44.277 --> 00:02:45.228
Thanks for watching!

00:02:45.648 --> 00:02:47.750
Every source is in the full article.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:48.350
I'm Pipkin.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:48.651
Bye!
